        "## 4. Train / Validation Split — why two sets?\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Training set** — the network *learns* from these images (it updates its weights on them).\n",
        "- **Validation set** — images the network **never trains on**. We use them only to *check* how well it does on unseen data.\n",
        "\n",
        "If a model does great on the training set but poorly on the validation set, it has **memorized** instead of **learned**. That gap is exactly what we will watch for.\n",
        "\n",
        "This dataset has **no predefined split**, so we create one ourselves: a **stratified 80% / 20% split** (stratified = every class keeps the same proportion in both sets, so the split is fair)."
      ],
      "id": "Rd4Z9R9DB8_h"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
